# Pages in a Word Document


The first page runs on and <!-- page: 2 -->continues here on the second page\.

<!-- page: 3 -->


The third page begins with a paragraph in a style that starts a page\.

This paragraph ends with a hard page break\.

<!-- page: 4 -->


The fourth page begins here\, once\, although two breaks mark it\.

The first section ends on the fourth page\.

<!-- page: i -->


The second section is numbered in lowercase Roman numerals\, and this is page i\.

This page ends here and <!-- page: ii -->page ii begins in the middle of a paragraph\.

